        "finding": "shape-gate-failure-recurrence",
        "findingDetail": "Submitted checker builds its verdicts object as a plain {} keyed by opaque per-run tokens via bracket assignment (verdicts[token] = ...). Assigning to the literal key \"__proto__\" on a plain object does not create an enumerable own property (hits Object.prototype's inherited accessor instead), so the checker's own JSON output is missing that one key, failing completeVerdicts()'s exact-key-count shape check and falling through to gradeChecker()'s synthetic all-failed fallback. This is the same defect class this package's own Trial 4 attempt exhibited, independently reproduced by a fresh, blind submission -- a recurrence of the defect class, not the same code."
